                <pb facs="0683" n="539" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg539"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.0146/117: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-24T17:00:00-05:00">April 24, 1929—5
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>135. Department’s #2, January 2, 6 p.m. Commander-in-Chief Asiatic Fleet is being
                    asked by Secretary of Navy for his opinion as to advisability under present
                    conditions of withdrawing all or part of marines now stationed in Shanghai.
                    Department would like to have your opinion regarding this. Opinion here is that
                    marines should be evacuated unless there is some controlling reason why they
                    should remain.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
